stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> authoring: gogo-plan creates .gogo/work/feature-slug/
  authoring --> authoring: analyst writes state.md / decisions.md / charts/
  authoring --> authoring: analyst dies mid-write (STAYS here - derived, crash-safe)
  authoring --> awaiting_acceptance: plan.md lands (present AND >= 2 '## ' sections)
  awaiting_acceptance --> plan_accepted: user accepts (in-chat, or m -> /gogo:accept)
  plan_accepted --> implementing: gogo-implement step 1 ENTRY write (else its exit write)
  implementing --> reviewing: gogo-review step 1 ENTRY write (else its exit write)
  reviewing --> testing: gogo-test step 1 ENTRY write (else its exit write)
  testing --> awaiting_uat: report 5
  implementing --> stalled: session killed, no live gogo-go
  stalled --> implementing: gogo go slug resumes (RunnableStatus is true)

  note right of authoring
    DERIVED, display-only. The status on disk
    is still awaiting-plan-acceptance (or
    absent); plan.md's absence or stub-ness is
    what makes it read as authoring. NO new
    status enum value, NO new class: it stays
    unfinished, in the plan column.
    Card: dim '✎ authoring', no gate stripe.
    m AND M refuse; gogo go and /gogo:accept
    refuse. Not counted in '⏸ K need you' nor
    in gogo status's WAIT column. The refusal
    names its number and its unblock.
  end note

  note right of plan_accepted
    TWO writers move this line, on purpose:
    each phase writes phase/status at its
    START (accurate when it fires) and AGAIN
    at its END. 0.29.0 briefly dropped the exit
    write, and state.md then stopped advancing
    at all - the entry write is prose an LLM
    follows and was skipped on all 3 live runs.
    Floor = one phase behind, ceiling = live.

    BEFORE 0.29.0 the whole build ran INSIDE
    this state: gogo-implement wrote
    implementing only at its step 4, after the
    work. The card sat in the plan column,
    in-progress read 0, the agent chip read
    '● analyst', and the cap did NOT count it -
    so a second build could clobber the tree.
    Now: the phases write at ENTRY, and the cap
    counts a live gogo-go session regardless of
    the file-derived class. A card in the
    residual launch-to-first-write window shows
    an amber '● building' cue and keeps its
    file-derived column.
  end note

  note right of stalled
    Not a status on disk - a DERIVED cue: a
    working status (implementing / reviewing /
    testing) with no live session for the slug.
    The cost of an honest entry write is that a
    killed phase leaves 'implementing' behind,
    so it must read '· stalled' rather than
    running. Quiet glyph: it is resumable.

    A SECOND derived cue covers the opposite
    writer failure - a phase that starts and
    forgets to record itself (observed live on
    this very feature's review round). When the
    newest event is a phase-done for the phase
    state.md still names AND a build session is
    live, the phase line is provably behind:
    the card reads '· state lags'. So a skipped
    entry write is visible, never silent.
  end note
